# Fault.Bounds drop-correctness (error-model.md §11 §5): a faultable array read
# of a Drop-bearing element (String). The Bounds handler branch lives in the
# GIR/LIR CFG so drop-insertion runs over it; the in-bounds read borrows/clones
# the element and the out-of-bounds read takes the handler — both ASan-clean
# (no leak, no double-free of the Vector's owned strings).
void main():
    Vector[String] names = ["alice", "bob", "carol"]
    # In-bounds: yields the element.
    String a = (names[1]) catch Fault.Bounds: "out-of-range"
    print(a)
    # Out-of-bounds: takes the handler, yields the fallback. The Vector's owned
    # strings are still dropped exactly once at scope end.
    String b = (names[9]) catch Fault.Bounds: "out-of-range"
    print(b)
